    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS \u2014 the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `registrationDate` feature on owner creation (`POST /api/owners`), returning it in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format and defaulting it to the server's current date when not supplied.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `registrationDate` field (`type: string`, `format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema, so it flows into the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` as a `LocalDate` and is Jackson-serialized as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `registrationDate` (`LocalDate`) field mapped to a `registration_date` column, with getter/setter. MapStruct maps it by name automatically in both directions.\n\n3. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 In `addOwner`, default the registration date to `LocalDate.now()` when the client omits it; a supplied date is preserved.\n\n4. **Schema files** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres` `schema.sql`) \u2014 Added the nullable `registration_date DATE` column (tests run on the hsqldb profile with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column must exist in the script).\n\n5. **`db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 The seed owners use positional `INSERT ... VALUES`, so I appended a `NULL` registration date to each of the 10 rows to keep the column count matched (the other dialects' seed files use explicit column lists and needed no change).\n\nBoth acceptance tests pass: `coreDefaultsToToday` (defaults to today) and `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate` (keeps `2020-06-15`).",
